{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":2,"output":8,"cacheRead":14303,"cacheWrite":2258,"totalTokens":16571,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.000004,"cacheRead":0.00014303,"cacheWrite":0.00028225,"total":0.00042948,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"I'm weighing a Badge design that yields Segments from __rich_console__. Building a Text object and rendering it would be simplest, though it might wrap, so I'm also considering whether to construct the Segment list directly and handle width truncation myself.\n\nStill writing the Text object with border spans...\n\nStill writing the Text object, now setting its left and right border parts with the icon and content in between.\n\nChecking how a standalone print ends the line: Console.print adds no trailing newline for a plain renderable, so a Badge with an empty end would leave the cursor mid-line. Table cells are different, since a newline there would break the row, so the choice of end value has to work for both cases.\n\nI'm settling on a Text object as the render, with no-wrap and ellipsis so the badge truncates instead of breaking across lines. For a standalone print, the default trailing newline in Text is the right end value, and it should behave the same inside a table cell.\n\nMeasurement is handled by the Panel, which asks the child for its size using the options, and the maximum here is just the total width. I'm weighing whether to yield a Text object directly so that no_wrap and ellipsis handle truncation, or to yield raw Segments, and Text is simpler and keeps the render stateless with respect to options.\n\nMeasurement could be clamped to the available width, but Console.measure already does that, so returning the exact total should be enough. I'm also wondering whether the cell_len call on the body should sit alongside the Text width check.\n\nI'm checking whether rich/__init__.py needs an eager import of Badge, since the existing module doesn't import from its submodules and a top-level import could cause a circular dependency through text and console.\n\nChecking the module-level `__getattr__` approach for `Badge`: it keeps `import rich` fast, and `__all__` should list `Badge` so `from rich import *` still works.\n\nChecking the module docs next, then I'm going to verify `Text.assemble`'s signature in the repo, since I'm fairly sure it takes `end=\"\\n\"` but want to confirm before writing the badge file and some tests for it.\n\n"}}
