{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":2,"output":687,"cacheRead":25559,"cacheWrite":232,"totalTokens":26480,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.0003435,"cacheRead":0.00025559,"cacheWrite":0.000029,"total":0.00062829,"totalFromProvider":true},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":72},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"`Badge` is implemented in `rich/badge.py`, exported from `rich` (including `__all__`), and has 6 new passing tests. The full suite shows 12 failures, but the untouched HEAD checkout has the same 12 (markdown, syntax, and card render tests), so they predate this change.\n\n**What it does**\n- `Badge(text, *, style, border_style, pill=True, icon=None)` renders `( OK )` for pills or `[ ALERT ]` for square badges, with `icon + \" \" + text` when an icon is given. This follows ADR-0002's one-space padding rule.\n- It is a renderable with `__rich_console__` (yields a `Text` built fresh per render, with `no_wrap` and ellipsis overflow) and `__rich_measure__` (width = cell length of both caps plus the body, so the 4 border/padding cells are counted).\n- It does not touch `console._buffer`, and it does not mutate `options`.\n\n**Verified**\n- Standalone `console.print(Badge(...))`, nested in a `Table` cell, and inside a `Panel` all render correctly.\n- Measurement is cell-based: `Badge(\"字\")` measures 6.\n- `import rich` does not load `rich.console`, because `Badge` is resolved lazily through a module-level `__getattr__`. `from rich import *` and `from rich import Badge` both work.\n\n**Notes**\n- `mypy` and `black` aren't installed in this environment, so I couldn't run the type check or formatting check. The code uses typed signatures and avoids `tuple[...]` for Python 3.8 compatibility.\n- The `.ki-base/` and `AGENTS.md` changes in `git status` were already there before I started; I didn't touch them.\n\nFiles: `rich/badge.py` (new), `rich/__init__.py` (edited), `tests/test_badge.py` (new)."}}
