{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"","sections":{"preamble":"You are a coding assistant running inside pi, a coding agent harness. Help users inspect files, run commands, and modify code.","tools":"<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n- grep: Search file contents for patterns (respects .gitignore)\n- find: Find files by glob pattern (respects .gitignore)\n- ls: List directory contents\n\nAdditional tools may be available.\n</tools>","rules":"<rules>\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for targeted changes. Batch changes to one file in a single call.\n- Each edits[].oldText must exactly and uniquely match the original file. Keep matches short and non-overlapping; merge nearby changes without including large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>","docs":"<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about the harness itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- Before implementing harness changes, read the relevant docs and examples in full, following related cross-references.\n</docs>","project_context":"<project_context>\nProject-specific instructions and guidelines:\n\n<project_instructions path=\"/app/AGENTS.md\">\n# AI Agent Guidelines (AGENTS.md) — Textualize/rich\n\n> Contributor and AI coding assistant guidelines for the **`Textualize/rich`** repository.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Project Philosophy & Architecture\n\nRich is a Python library for rich text and beautiful terminal formatting with zero non-standard runtime dependencies outside foundational typing and syntax parsers (`typing_extensions`, `pygments`, `markdown-it-py`).\n\n### Core Architectural Layers\n* **Console & Segments (`rich.console`, `rich.segment`)**:\n  - `Console` is the primary facade coordinating measurement, rendering, and terminal emission.\n  - `Segment` is the atomic rendering unit: a tuple of `(text: str, style: Optional[Style], control: Optional[ControlCode])`.\n* **Render Protocol (`rich.protocol`)**:\n  - Any renderable object implements `__rich_console__(self, console: Console, options: ConsoleOptions) -> RenderResult`.\n  - Generator method yielding `Segment` instances or nested renderables.\n  - Optional `__rich_measure__(self, console: Console, options: ConsoleOptions) -> Measurement` for computing minimum and maximum cell width.\n* **Style System (`rich.style`, `rich.color`, `rich.default_styles`)**:\n  - `Style` objects encapsulate ANSI SGR attributes (bold, italic, underline, color).\n  - Styles are immutable and combinable (`style1 + style2` or `Style.combine([s1, s2])`).\n  - Terminal themes map ANSI color names to RGB triplets.\n* **Layout & Data Structures (`rich.layout`, `rich.table`, `rich.panel`, `rich._ratio`)**:\n  - High-level containers (`Table`, `Panel`, `Columns`, `Tree`, `Layout`).\n  - `rich._ratio` provides mathematical solvers (`ratio_distribute`, `ratio_resolve`) for dividing available terminal cells among flexible and fixed-width components.\n* **Text & Markup (`rich.text`, `rich.markup`, `rich.highlighter`)**:\n  - `Text` manages character spans and styling offsets.\n  - `rich.markup` parses BBCode-like terminal markup (e.g., `[bold red]Alert[/]`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Engineering Standards & Conventions\n\n1. **Strict Type Annotations**:\n   - Every function, method parameter, and return type must have explicit Python type annotations (`typing`).\n   - Code must satisfy `mypy` without errors.\n2. **Pure Python & Zero Dependency Invariant**:\n   - Never introduce external third-party dependencies.\n   - Maintain compatibility across supported Python versions (3.8+).\n3. **Immutability & Stateless Rendering**:\n   - Do not mutate passed `ConsoleOptions` instances; use `options.update(...)` to derive child constraints.\n   - Never write directly to private console buffers (`console._buffer`). Always yield `Segment` instances.\n4. **Code Formatting**:\n   - Code adheres to standard `black` formatting and strict docstring conventions.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Testing & Verification Workflow\n\n`pytest` and all Rich dependencies are pre-installed in the environment. Always verify your changes using targeted `pytest` commands for the relevant module(s) before concluding your turn:\n\n```bash\n# Run ratio and table layout tests\npytest tests/test_ratio.py tests/test_table.py -q\n\n# Run styling and markup tests\npytest tests/test_style.py tests/test_markup.py -q\n\n# Run protocol and container tests\npytest tests/test_protocol.py tests/test_panel.py -q\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Architectural Knowledge Base (`ki-manager` MCP)\n\nThis repository is indexed by [**`ki-manager`**](https://github.com/Laeryid/KI-base), an active MCP server exposing curated Knowledge Items (KIs) and Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) with exact file locations, line ranges, and architectural invariants.\n\n### Available MCP Tools (Direct Exposure)\n- `mcp__ki_manager__ki_search`: BM25 search across all KIs and ADRs (`query`, `scope=\"all\"|\"ki\"|\"adr\"`, `limit`).\n- `mcp__ki_manager__ki_read`: Read a specific KI or ADR by filename (`rel_path`, optional `section`).\n- `mcp__ki_manager__ki_list`: List all registered KIs and ADRs (`scope=\"all\"|\"ki\"|\"adr\"`).\n- `mcp__ki_manager__ki_instructions`: Retrieve workflow instructions (`document=\"overview\"|\"knowledge-items\"`).\n\n### Mandatory Agent Workflow\n1. **Query `ki-manager` FIRST (Before Reading Source Code)**:\n   - Always start your task by calling `mcp__ki_manager__ki_search(query=\"...\")` or `mcp__ki_manager__ki_read(rel_path=\"...\")` for the relevant KI and ADR from the tables below.\n   - The Knowledge Items contain **exact line numbers and method invariants** (e.g. `L523–L585` in `rich/table.py` or `L2342–L2415` in `rich/console.py`).\n2. **Use Targeted File Reads (`offset` / `limit`)**:\n   - Once `mcp__ki_manager__ki_read` gives you the exact line numbers and invariants, use `read(path=\"...\", offset=..., limit=...)` to inspect only the target lines instead of reading entire 1,000–2,600 line files.\n   - Always ensure your changes strictly comply with the relevant ADRs (`0001`–`0004`).\n\n### Knowledge Items Manifest\n\n| File | Topic / Summary |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| `KI_rich_align.md` | Central pipeline of Rich: houses the primary `Console` class, ANSI escape sequence decoder, cell width calculators, border box constants, and alignment/column containers. It coordinates measurement, rendering, and terminal stream emission. |\n| `KI_rich_default.md` | Houses split-screen terminal layout panes (`Layout`), pattern regex highlighters (`Highlighter`), JSON syntax formatters, Rich logging handlers (`RichHandler`), default theme color rules, and Jupyter notebook rendering shims. |\n| `KI_rich_emoji.md` | Provides core emoji parsing, color representation (RGB/triplets/ANSI palettes), Windows console detection/rendering, and library top-level entry points. It translates high-level text embellishments and color palettes into terminal-safe output. |\n| `KI_rich_live.md` | Manages dynamic terminal updates, animations, multi-task progress bars, HTML/SVG export templates, and IPython integration. It allows real-time interactive terminal applications to refresh without screen scrolling. |\n| `KI_rich_markdown.md` | Provides markdown document parsing, console markup parsing (`[bold red]...[/]`), framed panel containers (`Panel`), recursive object pretty-printing (`Pretty`), user interactive prompts (`Prompt`), and the Rich Console Protocol definitions. |\n| `KI_rich_null.md` | Provides internal mathematical routines, layout ratio solvers, text wrapping primitives, platform Win32 console structures, and base ABC protocols. It forms the low-level foundation for rendering algorithms. |\n| `KI_rich_region.md` | Defines the atomic rendering primitives of Rich: `Segment` (minimal text+style tuple), `Style` (ANSI attributes container), `Rule` (horizontal dividing lines), `Status` (loading indicators with spinners), and alternate screen buffer controls (`Screen`). |\n| `KI_rich_syntax.md` | Implements high-level data presentation components: `Table` (grid formatting with auto-wrapping), `Text` (styled character spans), `Syntax` (Pygments code highlighting), `Traceback` (rich exception rendering), and `Tree` (hierarchical tree visualizations). |\n| `KI_rich_unicode11-0-0.md` | Contains precomputed Unicode East Asian Width lookup tables for modern Unicode specifications (versions 11.0.0 through 17.0.0, plus 4.1.0). These tables determine whether individual Unicode codepoints occupy 0, 1, or 2 terminal character cells. |\n| `KI_rich_unicode5-0-0.md` | Stores precomputed character width lookup tables for historical Unicode versions (versions 5.0.0 through 9.0.0). It provides backward-compatible East Asian Width measurements for legacy terminal environments and older OS consoles. |\n| `_OVERVIEW.ki.md` | Architectural master blueprint, layer boundaries, and core design invariants of the Rich library. |\n\n### Architecture Decision Records (ADRs)\n\n| ID | Title | Status | Date | File |\n| :---: | :--- | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| **0001** | Terminal Segments & Atomic Decomposition | Accepted | 2026-11-08 | `.ki-base/decisions/0001-terminal-segments.md` |\n| **0002** | Render Protocol & Component Isolation | Accepted | 2026-11-08 | `.ki-base/decisions/0002-render-protocol.md` |\n| **0003** | Style Composition & ANSI Sequences | Accepted | 2026-11-08 | `.ki-base/decisions/0003-style-composition-and-ansi.md` |\n| **0004** | Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation | Accepted | 2026-11-08 | `.ki-base/decisions/0004-ratio-distribution-and-layout.md` |\n\n</project_instructions>\n</project_context>","cwd":"<cwd>\n/app\n</cwd>"},"timestamp":1794168150760,"toolsAdded":[{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}}},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"grep","description":"Search file contents for a pattern. Returns matching lines with file paths and line numbers. Respects .gitignore. Output is truncated to 100 matches or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Long lines are truncated to 500 chars.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["pattern"],"properties":{"pattern":{"type":"string","description":"Search pattern (regex or literal string)"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"Directory or file to search (default: current directory)"},"glob":{"type":"string","description":"Filter files by glob pattern, e.g. '*.ts' or '**/*.spec.ts'"},"ignoreCase":{"type":"boolean","description":"Case-insensitive search (default: false)"},"literal":{"type":"boolean","description":"Treat pattern as literal string instead of regex (default: false)"},"context":{"type":"number","description":"Number of lines to show before and after each match (default: 0)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of matches to return (default: 100)"}}}},{"name":"find","description":"Search for files by glob pattern. Returns matching file paths relative to the search directory. Respects .gitignore. Output is truncated to 1000 results or 50KB (whichever is hit first).","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["pattern"],"properties":{"pattern":{"type":"string","description":"Glob pattern to match files, e.g. '*.ts', '**/*.json', or 'src/**/*.spec.ts'"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"Directory to search in (default: current directory)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of results (default: 1000)"}}}},{"name":"ls","description":"List directory contents. Returns entries sorted alphabetically, with '/' suffix for directories. Includes dotfiles. Output is truncated to 500 entries or 50KB (whichever is hit first).","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Directory to list (default: current directory)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of entries to return (default: 500)"}}}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_instructions","description":"Get workflow instructions and project rules for ki-manager. Available documents:\n- 'overview' — global AI rules and project navigation\n- 'knowledge-items' — table of registered KI files\n- 'create-adr' — workflow: document architectural decisions\n- 'expand-knowledge' — workflow: deep enrichment of KI files\n- 'scaffold-knowledge' — workflow: bulk scaffold of uncovered modules\n- 'sync-knowledge' — workflow: sync KI after code changes\nCall this before starting any documentation workflow task.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"document":{"type":"string","description":"Document name from the list above (e.g. 'create-adr')"}},"required":["document"]}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_list","description":"List Knowledge Items (KI) and Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) registered in the active project. Provides a structured overview of all documented modules, topics, and architectural decisions.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"scope":{"type":"string","enum":["all","ki","adr"],"default":"all","description":"Filter by document type: 'all' (default), 'ki' (Knowledge Items), or 'adr' (Architecture Decision Records)."},"format":{"type":"string","enum":["markdown","json"],"default":"markdown","description":"Output format: 'markdown' (structured tables, default) or 'json'."},"filter":{"type":"string","description":"Optional substring to filter by filename, title, summary, or covered module."}}}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_search","description":"Search Knowledge Items (KI) and ADRs by keywords using BM25 ranking (pure Python). Returns matching paths, titles, relevance scores, and text snippets. Use this tool to find relevant documentation without full codebase scans.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string","description":"Search query keywords (e.g. 'workspace detection' or 'dependency management')."},"scope":{"type":"string","enum":["all","ki","adr"],"default":"all","description":"Scope of search: 'all' (default), 'ki' (knowledge items), or 'adr' (architecture decision records)."},"limit":{"type":"integer","default":5,"description":"Maximum number of results to return (default: 5)."},"offset":{"type":"integer","default":0,"description":"Result offset for pagination (default: 0)."},"page":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"default":1,"description":"Page number for pagination (1-based, alternative to offset)."},"format":{"type":"string","enum":["markdown","json"],"default":"markdown","description":"Output format: 'markdown' (compact list, default) or 'json'."}},"required":["query"]}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","description":"Read a Knowledge Item (KI) or ADR markdown file. Supports optional section filtering (by markdown header), character limits, and offset.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"rel_path":{"type":"string","description":"Path or filename of the Knowledge Item or ADR (e.g. 'KI_architecture.md', 'knowledge/KI_architecture.md', or '001_some.md')."},"section":{"type":"string","description":"Optional markdown section title to extract (e.g. 'Architecture' or 'Known Issues')."},"max_chars":{"type":"integer","description":"Optional maximum number of characters to return (truncates if exceeded)."},"offset":{"type":"integer","default":0,"description":"Optional character offset to start reading from (default: 0)."}},"required":["rel_path"]}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_tools","description":"Inspect available ki-manager tools and their schemas. Call without arguments to list all tools grouped by category. Provide 'name' to inspect the exact inputSchema of a specific tool before calling it via ki_call or ki_mutate.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"Optional tool name to get full JSON schema (e.g. 'audit_coverage')."},"group":{"type":"string","description":"Optional category group filter (init_registry, coverage_analysis, scaffold, config_adr, files, git_state)."}}}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_call","description":"Execute a read-only ki-manager tool. Available tools: analyze_all_dependencies, analyze_dependencies, analyze_module, audit_coverage, check_ki_drift, find_unmapped_files, generate_dir_index, git_diff_secured, ki_graph_visualize, ki_list_projects, ki_scaffold_status, ki_split_analyze, ki_status, read_know_file. Use ki_tools(name=...) to check arguments. For mutating operations, use ki_mutate.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"tool":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the read-only tool to call.","enum":["analyze_all_dependencies","analyze_dependencies","analyze_module","audit_coverage","check_ki_drift","find_unmapped_files","generate_dir_index","git_diff_secured","ki_graph_visualize","ki_list_projects","ki_scaffold_status","ki_split_analyze","ki_status","read_know_file"]},"args":{"type":"object","description":"Arguments dictionary to pass to the tool.","default":{}}},"required":["tool"]}},{"name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_mutate","description":"Execute a state-modifying ki-manager tool. Available tools: add_ki_to_config, create_adr, edit_doc_config, edit_know_file, git_checkpoint, git_restore, ki_finalize_scaffolds, ki_init_project, ki_migrate_project, ki_prune_registry, ki_register_project, ki_scaffold, ki_split, make_know_dir, restore_mapping, save_state, sync_agents_md, update_last_verified, write_know_file. Use ki_tools(name=...) to check arguments.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"tool":{"type":"string","description":"Name of the mutating tool to call.","enum":["add_ki_to_config","create_adr","edit_doc_config","edit_know_file","git_checkpoint","git_restore","ki_finalize_scaffolds","ki_init_project","ki_migrate_project","ki_prune_registry","ki_register_project","ki_scaffold","ki_split","make_know_dir","restore_mapping","save_state","sync_agents_md","update_last_verified","write_know_file"]},"args":{"type":"object","description":"Arguments dictionary to pass to the tool.","default":{}}},"required":["tool"]}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Component Implementation: Embeddable `Badge` UI Component\n\nProblem Description:\nDevelop a new visual status badge component `Badge` in `rich/badge.py` (and export it in `rich/__init__.py` and `rich.__all__`).\nThe component must be fully compatible with Rich's layout and rendering pipeline so that it can be printed directly via `console.print(badge)` or embedded seamlessly inside Tables, Panels, Columns, and Trees.\n\nArchitectural Standard:\nThe component must strictly adhere to the internal architectural conventions of this repository (as documented in the project Architecture Decision Records). It must implement the standard streaming render protocol and measurement protocol accepted in the codebase, properly handling standalone and nested layouts without breaking composition or accessing private console state.\n\nRequirements:\n1. Create `rich/badge.py`:\n   - Class `Badge`:\n     ```python\n     def __init__(\n         self,\n         text: str,\n         *,\n         style: StyleType = \"bold white on blue\",\n         border_style: StyleType = \"blue\",\n         pill: bool = True,\n         icon: Optional[str] = None,\n     ) -> None:\n     ```\n   - When `pill=True`, formats the badge with curved pill borders `( ` ... ` )`.\n   - When `pill=False`, formats with square borders `[ ` ... ` ]`.\n   - If `icon` is provided, includes `icon + \" \" + text`.\n   - Accurately reports cell measurement based on character cell lengths.\n2. In `rich/__init__.py`:\n   - Expose `Badge` in `__all__` and make it importable from the top-level `rich` package.\n3. Verification:\n   - Must comply with project architectural standards and render cleanly when printed standalone or nested inside Tables and Panels.\n   - All existing tests must continue to pass without regressions."}],"timestamp":1794168150759},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'll start by checking the KI manager, as AGENTS.md asks, and I'll read ADRs 0001 and 0002 at the same time while I look at the rich package files.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll check the ADRs and the existing package layout before writing anything."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_018WiAHnTZPjYvLQ436PZytm","name":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_search","arguments":{"query":"render protocol measurement segments protocol component","scope":"adr"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01ErURjYpXuDZFkBFYjQ8mJp","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/app/rich/__init__.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_018DsA9ZHJxMpDgG5rgdd4fG","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /app && ls rich | head -100 && git status --short | head && cat .ki-base/decisions/0002-render-protocol.md 2>/dev/null | head -80"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5","usage":{"input":4,"output":381,"cacheRead":9448,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":9833,"cost":{"input":4.0000000000000003e-7,"output":0.0001905,"cacheRead":0.00009448,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00028538,"totalFromProvider":true},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":115},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794168150802,"providerThinkingLevel":"medium","responseId":"msg_011Cgr4KVY7VzuVJj7RJJyqg","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":2090,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_018WiAHnTZPjYvLQ436PZytm","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 4 result(s) for \"render protocol measurement segments protocol component\" [Page 1/1 (showing 1-4)]:\n\n1. [ADR] **ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation** (`.ki-base/decisions/0002-render-protocol.md`, score: 8.862)\n   > # ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation - **Status:** Accepted - **Date:** 2026-11-08 - **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers ## Context Rich supports...\n2. [ADR] **ADR-0001: Terminal Segments & Atomic Decomposition** (`.ki-base/decisions/0001-terminal-segments.md`, score: 3.42)\n   > # ADR-0001: Terminal Segments & Atomic Decomposition - **Status:** Accepted - **Date:** 2026-11-08 - **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers ## Context Terminal emulators...\n3. [ADR] **ADR-0003: Style Composition & ANSI Sequences** (`.ki-base/decisions/0003-style-composition-and-ansi.md`, score: 0.109)\n   > ...`rich/_export_format.py`) for SVG and HTML rendering. ## Consequences - Full consistency between CLI console output, HTML export, and SVG snapshots. - Guarantees predictable cascading style resolution...\n4. [ADR] **ADR-0004: Ratio Distribution & Column Allocation** (`.ki-base/decisions/0004-ratio-distribution-and-layout.md`, score: 0.106)\n   > ...Rich Architectural Maintainers ## Context When rendering tables and multi-pane split layouts, columns and panels have competing size constraints: minimum width, maximum width, fixed cell counts, or..."}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_search"},"isError":false,"durationMs":50,"timestamp":1794168157672},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01ErURjYpXuDZFkBFYjQ8mJp","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"\"\"Rich text and beautiful formatting in the terminal.\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nfrom typing import IO, TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Callable, Optional, Union\n\nfrom ._extension import load_ipython_extension  # noqa: F401\n\n__all__ = [\"get_console\", \"reconfigure\", \"print\", \"inspect\", \"print_json\"]\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from .console import Console\n\n# Global console used by alternative print\n_console: Optional[\"Console\"] = None\n\ntry:\n    _IMPORT_CWD = os.path.abspath(os.getcwd())\nexcept FileNotFoundError:\n    # Can happen if the cwd has been deleted\n    _IMPORT_CWD = \"\"\n\n\ndef get_console() -> \"Console\":\n    \"\"\"Get a global :class:`~rich.console.Console` instance. This function is used when Rich requires a Console,\n    and hasn't been explicitly given one.\n\n    Returns:\n        Console: A console instance.\n    \"\"\"\n    global _console\n    if _console is None:\n        from .console import Console\n\n        _console = Console()\n\n    return _console\n\n\ndef reconfigure(*args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Reconfigures the global console by replacing it with another.\n\n    Args:\n        *args (Any): Positional arguments for the replacement :class:`~rich.console.Console`.\n        **kwargs (Any): Keyword arguments for the replacement :class:`~rich.console.Console`.\n    \"\"\"\n    from rich.console import Console\n\n    new_console = Console(*args, **kwargs)\n    _console = get_console()\n    _console.__dict__ = new_console.__dict__\n\n\ndef print(\n    *objects: Any,\n    sep: str = \" \",\n    end: str = \"\\n\",\n    file: Optional[IO[str]] = None,\n    flush: bool = False,\n) -> None:\n    r\"\"\"Print object(s) supplied via positional arguments.\n    This function has an identical signature to the built-in print.\n    For more advanced features, see the :class:`~rich.console.Console` class.\n\n    Args:\n        sep (str, optional): Separator between printed objects. Defaults to \" \".\n        end (str, optional): Character to write at end of output. Defaults to \"\\\\n\".\n        file (IO[str], optional): File to write to, or None for stdout. Defaults to None.\n        flush (bool, optional): Has no effect as Rich always flushes output. Defaults to False.\n\n    \"\"\"\n    from .console import Console\n\n    write_console = get_console() if file is None else Console(file=file)\n    return write_console.print(*objects, sep=sep, end=end)\n\n\ndef print_json(\n    json: Optional[str] = None,\n    *,\n    data: Any = None,\n    indent: Union[None, int, str] = 2,\n    highlight: bool = True,\n    skip_keys: bool = False,\n    ensure_ascii: bool = False,\n    check_circular: bool = True,\n    allow_nan: bool = True,\n    default: Optional[Callable[[Any], Any]] = None,\n    sort_keys: bool = False,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Pretty prints JSON. Output will be valid JSON.\n\n    Args:\n        json (str): A string containing JSON.\n        data (Any): If json is not supplied, then encode this data.\n        indent (int, optional): Number of spaces to indent. Defaults to 2.\n        highlight (bool, optional): Enable highlighting of output: Defaults to True.\n        skip_keys (bool, optional): Skip keys not of a basic type. Defaults to False.\n        ensure_ascii (bool, optional): Escape all non-ascii characters. Defaults to False.\n        check_circular (bool, optional): Check for circular references. Defaults to True.\n        allow_nan (bool, optional): Allow NaN and Infinity values. Defaults to True.\n        default (Callable, optional): A callable that converts values that can not be encoded\n            in to something that can be JSON encoded. Defaults to None.\n        sort_keys (bool, optional): Sort dictionary keys. Defaults to False.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    get_console().print_json(\n        json,\n        data=data,\n        indent=indent,\n        highlight=highlight,\n        skip_keys=skip_keys,\n        ensure_ascii=ensure_ascii,\n        check_circular=check_circular,\n        allow_nan=allow_nan,\n        default=default,\n        sort_keys=sort_keys,\n    )\n\n\ndef inspect(\n    obj: Any,\n    *,\n    console: Optional[\"Console\"] = None,\n    title: Optional[str] = None,\n    help: bool = False,\n    methods: bool = False,\n    docs: bool = True,\n    private: bool = False,\n    dunder: bool = False,\n    sort: bool = True,\n    all: bool = False,\n    value: bool = True,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Inspect any Python object.\n\n    * inspect(<OBJECT>) to see summarized info.\n    * inspect(<OBJECT>, methods=True) to see methods.\n    * inspect(<OBJECT>, help=True) to see full (non-abbreviated) help.\n    * inspect(<OBJECT>, private=True) to see private attributes (single underscore).\n    * inspect(<OBJECT>, dunder=True) to see attributes beginning with double underscore.\n    * inspect(<OBJECT>, all=True) to see all attributes.\n\n    Args:\n        obj (Any): An object to inspect.\n        title (str, optional): Title to display over inspect result, or None use type. Defaults to None.\n        help (bool, optional): Show full help text rather than just first paragraph. Defaults to False.\n        methods (bool, optional): Enable inspection of callables. Defaults to False.\n        docs (bool, optional): Also render doc strings. Defaults to True.\n        private (bool, optional): Show private attributes (beginning with underscore). Defaults to False.\n        dunder (bool, optional): Show attributes starting with double underscore. Defaults to False.\n        sort (bool, optional):  Sort attributes alphabetically, callables at the top, leading and trailing underscores ignored. Defaults to True.\n        all (bool, optional): Show all attributes. Defaults to False.\n        value (bool, optional): Pretty print value. Defaults to True.\n    \"\"\"\n    _console = console or get_console()\n    from rich._inspect import Inspect\n\n    # Special case for inspect(inspect)\n    is_inspect = obj is inspect\n\n    _inspect = Inspect(\n        obj,\n        title=title,\n        help=is_inspect or help,\n        methods=is_inspect or methods,\n        docs=is_inspect or docs,\n        private=private,\n        dunder=dunder,\n        sort=sort,\n        all=all,\n        value=value,\n    )\n    _console.print(_inspect)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":  # pragma: no cover\n    print(\"Hello, **World**\")\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":28,"timestamp":1794168157674},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_018DsA9ZHJxMpDgG5rgdd4fG","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"__init__.py\n__main__.py\n__pycache__\n_emoji_codes.py\n_emoji_replace.py\n_export_format.py\n_extension.py\n_fileno.py\n_inspect.py\n_log_render.py\n_loop.py\n_null_file.py\n_palettes.py\n_pick.py\n_ratio.py\n_spinners.py\n_stack.py\n_timer.py\n_unicode_data\n_win32_console.py\n_windows.py\n_windows_renderer.py\n_wrap.py\nabc.py\nalign.py\nansi.py\nbar.py\nbox.py\ncells.py\ncolor.py\ncolor_triplet.py\ncolumns.py\nconsole.py\nconstrain.py\ncontainers.py\ncontrol.py\ndefault_styles.py\ndiagnose.py\nemoji.py\nerrors.py\nfile_proxy.py\nfilesize.py\nhighlighter.py\njson.py\njupyter.py\nlayout.py\nlive.py\nlive_render.py\nlogging.py\nmarkdown.py\nmarkup.py\nmeasure.py\npadding.py\npager.py\npalette.py\npanel.py\npretty.py\nprogress.py\nprogress_bar.py\nprompt.py\nprotocol.py\npy.typed\nregion.py\nrepr.py\nrule.py\nscope.py\nscreen.py\nsegment.py\nspinner.py\nstatus.py\nstyle.py\nstyled.py\nsyntax.py\ntable.py\nterminal_theme.py\ntext.py\ntheme.py\nthemes.py\ntraceback.py\ntree.py\n M .ki-base/DIR_INDEX.md\n M .ki-base/config.json\n M .ki-base/doc_config.json\n M .ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_align.md\n M .ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_null.md\n M .ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_region.md\n M .ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_syntax.md\n M AGENTS.md\n?? .ki-base/decisions/\n# ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nRich supports arbitrary nested UI components (such as Panels inside Tables inside Trees). If custom components were allowed to mutate shared rendering options or directly manipulate the `Console` buffer, rendering would become non-deterministic, thread-unsafe, and incompatible with real-time displays like `Live` and `Progress`.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Mandatory Console Protocol:**  \n   All visual components must implement the public generator protocol:\n   ```python\n   def __rich_console__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> \"RenderResult\":\n       ...\n       yield Segment(...)\n   ```\n   A component may optionally implement `__rich_measure__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> Measurement` for dynamic sizing.\n\n2. **Strict Component Isolation Invariants:**\n   - **No Buffer Access:** Components must NEVER access or write to `console._buffer` or `console.file` directly. All output must be returned via `yield` as an iterable of `Segment` or renderable objects.\n   - **Options Immutability:** The passed `options: ConsoleOptions` instance is strictly read-only. Components must never mutate its fields. To adjust constraints for child components, use `options.update(...)` which returns a fresh copy.\n   - **Stateless Yielding:** Generators must be re-entrant and idempotent so that multiple render passes (e.g. measuring then rendering) produce identical results without side effects.\n\n3. **Internal Spacing Convention for Inline Badges:**\n   - In accordance with repository design conventions, inline badge components must enclose their inner text with exactly one space of padding inside the boundary caps: `\"( \"` + content + `\" )\"` for pill badges, and `\"[\" + \" \"` + content + `\" ]\"` for square badges.\n   - Example: `Badge(\"DEPLOYED\", pill=True, icon=\"★\")` must yield segments rendering as `\"( ★ DEPLOYED )\"`. Square badges render as `\"[ SYSTEM ALERT ]\"`. Measurement must include the 4 cells occupied by borders and inner spaces.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Components can be composed arbitrarily without side effects.\n- Direct console buffer writes or mutating shared options is treated as an architectural violation and rejected in code review.\n- Ensures seamless integration with `Live` displays and virtual screen buffers.\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":4770,"timestamp":1794168157684},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking that the pill's four extra cells from the ADR hold up, and then looking at the Measurement class and a sample module like align.py before reading measure.py and cells.py.\n\nI'm going to check whether any tests enumerate the modules or verify `__all__`, so I'll read ADR 0001 and search for those.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"The ADR sets a concrete spacing rule: one space inside each cap, and measurement must count the 4 border/padding cells. I'll check ADR 0001, the measurement helpers, and whether any test enumerates `rich` exports."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01ErCSoXLkjaKCRpTSVusuqF","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /app && sed -n 1,80p .ki-base/decisions/0001-terminal-segments.md; echo ---; cat rich/measure.py | head -60; echo ---; grep -rn \"__all__\" tests | head; echo ---; grep -n \"def cell_len\" -A3 rich/cells.py; echo ---; sed -n 1,40p rich/rule.py"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5","usage":{"input":2,"output":457,"cacheRead":9448,"cacheWrite":4855,"totalTokens":14762,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.0002285,"cacheRead":0.00009448,"cacheWrite":0.000606875,"total":0.000930055,"totalFromProvider":true},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":211},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794168157698,"providerThinkingLevel":"medium","responseId":"msg_011Cgr4KzuhKMEcWLmk8e3LZ","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":2821,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01ErCSoXLkjaKCRpTSVusuqF","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0001: Terminal Segments & Atomic Decomposition\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nTerminal emulators operate on streams of characters interspersed with ANSI escape codes for styling and cursor movement. Without a unified primitive abstraction, high-level components (tables, syntax, markdown) would have to manually track escape codes, calculate visual cell widths, and handle cross-platform line breaks, leading to exponential complexity and bugs.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Atomic Segment Primitive:**  \n   Every visual element in Rich must ultimately reduce to a stream of `Segment` instances:\n   ```python\n   class Segment(NamedTuple):\n       text: str\n       style: Optional[Style] = None\n       control: Optional[Sequence[ControlCode]] = None\n   ```\n2. **Strict Invariants:**\n   - A `Segment` text piece must not contain unescaped newline characters `\\n` or `\\r` unless processed by `Segment.split_lines()` or `Segment.split_and_crop_lines()`.\n   - Visual measurement is derived strictly from `cell_len(segment.text)` using East Asian Width Unicode tables, never raw `len(text)`.\n   - Control sequences (cursor up, color palette queries) are encapsulated in the optional `control` field and take zero visual cell length.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- All rendering operations are stateless stream-processing pipelines.\n- Layout algorithms only need to measure and slice `Segment` collections.\n- Clean separation between logical layout calculation and physical terminal escape emission.\n---\nfrom operator import itemgetter\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Callable, NamedTuple, Optional, Sequence\n\nfrom . import errors\nfrom .protocol import is_renderable, rich_cast\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from .console import Console, ConsoleOptions, RenderableType\n\n\nclass Measurement(NamedTuple):\n    \"\"\"Stores the minimum and maximum widths (in characters) required to render an object.\"\"\"\n\n    minimum: int\n    \"\"\"Minimum number of cells required to render.\"\"\"\n    maximum: int\n    \"\"\"Maximum number of cells required to render.\"\"\"\n\n    @property\n    def span(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Get difference between maximum and minimum.\"\"\"\n        return self.maximum - self.minimum\n\n    def normalize(self) -> \"Measurement\":\n        \"\"\"Get measurement that ensures that minimum <= maximum and minimum >= 0\n\n        Returns:\n            Measurement: A normalized measurement.\n        \"\"\"\n        minimum, maximum = self\n        minimum = min(max(0, minimum), maximum)\n        return Measurement(max(0, minimum), max(0, max(minimum, maximum)))\n\n    def with_maximum(self, width: int) -> \"Measurement\":\n        \"\"\"Get a RenderableWith where the widths are <= width.\n\n        Args:\n            width (int): Maximum desired width.\n\n        Returns:\n            Measurement: New Measurement object.\n        \"\"\"\n        minimum, maximum = self\n        return Measurement(min(minimum, width), min(maximum, width))\n\n    def with_minimum(self, width: int) -> \"Measurement\":\n        \"\"\"Get a RenderableWith where the widths are >= width.\n\n        Args:\n            width (int): Minimum desired width.\n\n        Returns:\n            Measurement: New Measurement object.\n        \"\"\"\n        minimum, maximum = self\n        width = max(0, width)\n        return Measurement(max(minimum, width), max(maximum, width))\n\n    def clamp(\n        self, min_width: Optional[int] = None, max_width: Optional[int] = None\n---\n---\n98:def cell_len(text: str, unicode_version: str = \"auto\") -> int:\n99-    \"\"\"Get the cell length of a string (length as it appears in the terminal).\n100-\n101-    Args:\n---\nfrom typing import Union\n\nfrom .align import AlignMethod\nfrom .cells import cell_len, set_cell_size\nfrom .console import Console, ConsoleOptions, RenderResult\nfrom .jupyter import JupyterMixin\nfrom .measure import Measurement\nfrom .style import Style\nfrom .text import Text\n\n\nclass Rule(JupyterMixin):\n    \"\"\"A console renderable to draw a horizontal rule (line).\n\n    Args:\n        title (Union[str, Text], optional): Text to render in the rule. Defaults to \"\".\n        characters (str, optional): Character(s) used to draw the line. Defaults to \"─\".\n        style (StyleType, optional): Style of Rule. Defaults to \"rule.line\".\n        end (str, optional): Character at end of Rule. defaults to \"\\\\\\\\n\"\n        align (str, optional): How to align the title, one of \"left\", \"center\", or \"right\". Defaults to \"center\".\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        title: Union[str, Text] = \"\",\n        *,\n        characters: str = \"─\",\n        style: Union[str, Style] = \"rule.line\",\n        end: str = \"\\n\",\n        align: AlignMethod = \"center\",\n    ) -> None:\n        if cell_len(characters) < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\n                \"'characters' argument must have a cell width of at least 1\"\n            )\n        if align not in (\"left\", \"center\", \"right\"):\n            raise ValueError(\n                f'invalid value for align, expected \"left\", \"center\", \"right\" (not {align!r})'\n            )\n        self.title = title\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":205,"timestamp":1794168160727},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm weighing a Badge design that yields Segments from __rich_console__. Building a Text object and rendering it would be simplest, though it might wrap, so I'm also considering whether to construct the Segment list directly and handle width truncation myself.\n\nStill writing the Text object with border spans...\n\nStill writing the Text object, now setting its left and right border parts with the icon and content in between.\n\nChecking how a standalone print ends the line: Console.print adds no trailing newline for a plain renderable, so a Badge with an empty end would leave the cursor mid-line. Table cells are different, since a newline there would break the row, so the choice of end value has to work for both cases.\n\nI'm settling on a Text object as the render, with no-wrap and ellipsis so the badge truncates instead of breaking across lines. For a standalone print, the default trailing newline in Text is the right end value, and it should behave the same inside a table cell.\n\nMeasurement is handled by the Panel, which asks the child for its size using the options, and the maximum here is just the total width. I'm weighing whether to yield a Text object directly so that no_wrap and ellipsis handle truncation, or to yield raw Segments, and Text is simpler and keeps the render stateless with respect to options.\n\nMeasurement could be clamped to the available width, but Console.measure already does that, so returning the exact total should be enough. I'm also wondering whether the cell_len call on the body should sit alongside the Text width check.\n\nI'm checking whether rich/__init__.py needs an eager import of Badge, since the existing module doesn't import from its submodules and a top-level import could cause a circular dependency through text and console.\n\nChecking the module-level `__getattr__` approach for `Badge`: it keeps `import rich` fast, and `__all__` should list `Badge` so `from rich import *` still works.\n\nChecking the module docs next, then I'm going to verify `Text.assemble`'s signature in the repo, since I'm fairly sure it takes `end=\"\\n\"` but want to confirm before writing the badge file and some tests for it.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"Plan, following ADR-0001/0002: `Badge` builds a `Text` per render (no state mutation, no buffer access), uses `cell_len` for measurement, and counts the 4 border/padding cells. I'll expose it through a lazy module `__getattr__` in `rich/__init__.py`, which keeps `import rich` cheap, as the existing lazy helpers do."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01K9dAjdcp3DKKzSc25C8cfc","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/app/rich/badge.py","content":"from typing import Optional\n\nfrom .cells import cell_len\nfrom .console import Console, ConsoleOptions, RenderResult\nfrom .jupyter import JupyterMixin\nfrom .measure import Measurement\nfrom .style import Style, StyleType\nfrom .text import Text\n\n\nclass Badge(JupyterMixin):\n    \"\"\"A compact, embeddable status badge rendered as a pill or square box.\n\n    Args:\n        text (str): Text displayed inside the badge.\n        style (StyleType, optional): Style of the badge content. Defaults to \"bold white on blue\".\n        border_style (StyleType, optional): Style of the border caps. Defaults to \"blue\".\n        pill (bool, optional): Use curved pill caps ``( ... )`` if True, or square caps ``[ ... ]`` if False. Defaults to True.\n        icon (str, optional): Optional icon displayed before the text, separated by a space. Defaults to None.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    LEFT_PILL = \"( \"\n    RIGHT_PILL = \" )\"\n    LEFT_SQUARE = \"[ \"\n    RIGHT_SQUARE = \" ]\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        text: str,\n        *,\n        style: StyleType = \"bold white on blue\",\n        border_style: StyleType = \"blue\",\n        pill: bool = True,\n        icon: Optional[str] = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        self.text = text\n        self.style = style\n        self.border_style = border_style\n        self.pill = pill\n        self.icon = icon\n\n    @property\n    def _caps(self) -> \"tuple[str, str]\":\n        \"\"\"The (left, right) border caps, including the inner padding space.\"\"\"\n        if self.pill:\n            return self.LEFT_PILL, self.RIGHT_PILL\n        return self.LEFT_SQUARE, self.RIGHT_SQUARE\n\n    @property\n    def _body(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"The content placed between the caps.\"\"\"\n        if self.icon:\n            return f\"{self.icon} {self.text}\"\n        return self.text\n\n    def _build_text(self) -> Text:\n        \"\"\"Build a fresh Text for each render pass, so rendering stays stateless.\"\"\"\n        left, right = self._caps\n        return Text.assemble(\n            (left, Style.pick_first(self.border_style, \"blue\") and self.border_style),\n            (self._body, self.style),\n            (right, self.border_style),\n            no_wrap=True,\n            overflow=\"ellipsis\",\n        )\n\n    def __rich_console__(\n        self, console: Co